Also, OP is using 3.3.4. [Godot 3.3.x is not supported for bug fixes anymore](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/about/release_policy.html#release-support-timeline), so please upgrade to [3.4.4](https://godotengine.org/article/maintenance-release-godot-3-4-4) and check if the issue still occurs there.

Could it be related to _gui_input? I remembered creating a custom carousel field. All action where trigged inside the _gui_input. But when using an analog stick, both action_pressed were trigger (both when using and released), resulting in a quite fast navigation

https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1162446/178615774-71f480de-c82c-4b0f-8bb6-f9cf6058299f.mp4

```
func _gui_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
	if event.is_action_pressed("ui_left"):
		_on_Previous_value()
		return

	if event.is_action_pressed("ui_right"):
		_on_Next_value()
		return
```

I fixed it by checking the raw strengh


```
func _gui_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
	if event is InputEventJoypadMotion:
		if event.get_action_strength("ui_left") == 1:
			_on_Previous_value()
			return
		if event.get_action_strength("ui_right") == 1:
			_on_Next_value()
			return
		return
	
	if event.is_action_pressed("ui_left"):
		_on_Previous_value()
		return

	if event.is_action_pressed("ui_right"):
		_on_Next_value()
		return
```

https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1162446/178615791-a9acd41c-6356-42d0-896b-dbc2c6129d6b.mp4

I saw the same behavior in `slider.cpp`

```
void Slider::_gui_input(Ref<InputEvent> p_event) {
	if (!editable) {
		return;
	}
	...
	if (!mm.is_valid() && !mb.is_valid()) {
		if (p_event->is_action_pressed("ui_left", true)) {
			if (orientation != HORIZONTAL) {
				return;
			}
			set_value(get_value() - (custom_step >= 0 ? custom_step : get_step()));
			accept_event();
		} else if (p_event->is_action_pressed("ui_right", true)) {
			if (orientation != HORIZONTAL) {
				return;
			}
			set_value(get_value() + (custom_step >= 0 ? custom_step : get_step()));
			accept_event();
		} else if (p_event->is_action_pressed("ui_up", true)) {
			if (orientation != VERTICAL) {
				return;
			}

			set_value(get_value() + (custom_step >= 0 ? custom_step : get_step()));
			accept_event();
		} else if (p_event->is_action_pressed("ui_down", true)) {
			if (orientation != VERTICAL) {
				return;
			}
			set_value(get_value() - (custom_step >= 0 ? custom_step : get_step()));
			accept_event();
		} else if (p_event->is_action("ui_home") && p_event->is_pressed()) {
			set_value(get_min());
			accept_event();
		} else if (p_event->is_action("ui_end") && p_event->is_pressed()) {
			set_value(get_max());
			accept_event();
		}
	}

```

Should we add someking of exception to check when an event input is of type `InputEventJoypadMotion ` ?
